WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.330 --> 00:00:02.070
- Let's welcome our
first guest, everybody.

00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:04.410
You have seen her in
"Ant-Man: Quantumania,"

00:00:04.410 --> 00:00:07.260
and you knew him from
"Riverdale," or you know him,

00:00:07.260 --> 00:00:09.600
you knew him, you know him,
all the things, all the tenses,

00:00:09.600 --> 00:00:11.400
and now you can see them together

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:12.960
in the movie "Lisa Frankenstein."

00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.250
It's in Theaters Friday.

00:00:14.250 --> 00:00:16.925
Please welcome Kathryn
Newton and Cole Sprouse.

00:00:16.925 --> 00:00:21.925
(all cheering)
(upbeat music)

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:45.090
Oh my gosh.

00:00:45.090 --> 00:00:46.890
- Not every day you do an
interview with a puppy.

00:00:46.890 --> 00:00:48.090
- [Kelly] I'm just, you're welcome.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:49.243
- Thank you, thank you, Kelly.

00:00:49.243 --> 00:00:51.150
- I love, you love dogs, you have three?

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:51.983
- [Kathryn] I have three.

00:00:51.983 --> 00:00:53.016
- Yeah?

00:00:53.016 --> 00:00:53.849
- I have three poodles.

00:00:53.849 --> 00:00:55.583
There's Jack King Ruler of All Fluff,

00:00:55.583 --> 00:00:57.900
Danford Ladybird Keep the Madness Rolling,

00:00:57.900 --> 00:01:00.720
and Starlight Rosebud Hella
Goodboy Gonna Need a Big Bank.

00:01:00.720 --> 00:01:02.069
This is Frost.

00:01:02.069 --> 00:01:02.910
- What?

00:01:02.910 --> 00:01:04.063
- [Kathryn] Yeah.
(audience laughing)

00:01:04.063 --> 00:01:05.760
- And what's this one's name, Snowflake?

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:07.980
- This is Snowflake, I chose Snowflake

00:01:07.980 --> 00:01:10.710
because she has the same bags
under her eyes that I do.

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:12.317
- [Kelly] You need sleep.

00:01:12.317 --> 00:01:14.987
- I said, "You're just as
tired as me, Snowflake.

00:01:14.987 --> 00:01:16.423
Let's do this thing."

00:01:16.423 --> 00:01:17.999
- Oh my God, so cute.

00:01:17.999 --> 00:01:21.103
So which dog is in this video, though?

00:01:21.103 --> 00:01:22.013
We have video right here.

00:01:22.013 --> 00:01:23.910
- [Kathryn] I think he just likes me.

00:01:23.910 --> 00:01:25.140
- [Kelly] Which dog is this?

00:01:25.140 --> 00:01:26.580
- That's Starlight Rosebud Hella Goodboy

00:01:26.580 --> 00:01:28.740
Gonna Need a Big Bank, his name's Buddy.

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:31.470
He doubles as my caddy on the side.

00:01:31.470 --> 00:01:32.910
He likes to chase birds,

00:01:32.910 --> 00:01:36.840
and my other dog, Jack,
professional golfer, okay?

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:38.700
He doesn't go to the
bathroom on the golf course.

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:39.570
- [Kelly] Okay.
- Pro,

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.280
and he will like fetch my golf ball

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.680
and bring it back to me
so I can just practice.

00:01:43.680 --> 00:01:44.790
- That's nice.
- Yeah.

00:01:44.790 --> 00:01:46.636
My big guy, he just chases everything.

00:01:46.636 --> 00:01:48.360
He thinks he's a real dog.

00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:51.150
- Do they usually allow,
I feel like I have golfed,

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:53.220
and I don't know that dogs were allowed

00:01:53.220 --> 00:01:54.270
to come on the golf course.

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:55.944
- They're probably not, but I think

00:01:55.944 --> 00:01:58.590
they just don't say anything.

00:01:58.590 --> 00:01:59.670
- That's very, you know what,

00:01:59.670 --> 00:02:01.830
you can always say sorry
later, do what you want.

00:02:01.830 --> 00:02:03.420
There you go, that's the goal, yeah.

00:02:03.420 --> 00:02:04.950
Wait, and here, Cole, this is you.

00:02:04.950 --> 00:02:06.540
This is your Pomeranian, right?

00:02:06.540 --> 00:02:07.550
- [Kathryn] Oh my God.

00:02:07.550 --> 00:02:08.980
(audience laughing)

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:12.210
- Look at the closeup
on that, it's amazing.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:13.236
What's your dog's name again?

00:02:13.236 --> 00:02:15.690
- That's Bear or Goose.

00:02:15.690 --> 00:02:17.400
- Bear or Goose, is it depending

00:02:17.400 --> 00:02:18.810
on the day or?
- One of the two.

00:02:18.810 --> 00:02:20.850
Unlike Kathryn's dogs,

00:02:20.850 --> 00:02:23.788
I don't think he has an
ounce of dog left in him.

00:02:23.788 --> 00:02:26.100
I think he is-
- [Kathryn] Bird?

00:02:26.100 --> 00:02:27.600
- Yeah, he's a little bit more bird,

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:30.320
like Goose, like a big goose.

00:02:30.320 --> 00:02:31.153
- Okay.

00:02:31.153 --> 00:02:32.460
- "Bear and Goose," actually,

00:02:32.460 --> 00:02:34.590
that's a book my son
loves to read, actually.

00:02:34.590 --> 00:02:35.729
That's amazing.

00:02:35.729 --> 00:02:37.272
This is kind of cool because sometimes

00:02:37.272 --> 00:02:38.370
when you're in movies
you don't know people,

00:02:38.370 --> 00:02:39.720
but y'all have been
friends for a while, right?

00:02:39.720 --> 00:02:40.830
- Yeah, long time.

00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:42.062
- Yeah, when did y'all meet?

00:02:42.062 --> 00:02:42.951
- Well.
(Kathryn laughs)

00:02:42.951 --> 00:02:44.220
- Well.

00:02:44.220 --> 00:02:45.300
- [Kelly] Do you have different stories?

00:02:45.300 --> 00:02:49.500
- Kathryn revealed to me only a month ago.

00:02:49.500 --> 00:02:51.660
- Oh, that's right, we
met a long time ago.

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:54.330
- That she asked for a
photo of my twin and I

00:02:54.330 --> 00:02:56.970
at Bob's Big Boy in Los Angeles.

00:02:56.970 --> 00:02:58.298
- I was around seven years old,

00:02:58.298 --> 00:03:01.410
huge fan, obviously, who wasn't, right?

00:03:01.410 --> 00:03:02.405
Everyone here is a fan.

00:03:02.405 --> 00:03:04.080
(audience cheering)

00:03:04.080 --> 00:03:06.000
And I'm lucky enough to be one

00:03:06.000 --> 00:03:08.880
of the people who got a
picture with the Sprouse twins.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:10.260
- I didn't remember the moment.

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:12.020
- No,
(audience laughs)

00:03:12.020 --> 00:03:14.160
and I didn't tell him about it
until way, way into filming,

00:03:14.160 --> 00:03:15.810
because I wanted to
like be cool, you know?

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:18.330
I wanted to be like we're both
actors, like we're the same.

00:03:18.330 --> 00:03:19.284
We're not the same.

00:03:19.284 --> 00:03:20.550
(all laughing)

00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:21.810
- We are equal.
- We are not the same,

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:22.643
not at all.

00:03:22.643 --> 00:03:24.450
- Well, you did a photo shoot with,

00:03:24.450 --> 00:03:25.530
because I mean, he's a photographer.

00:03:25.530 --> 00:03:28.170
We talked about this last
time, but you did a photo shoot

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:29.880
with him, and it kind
of was like inspiring

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:31.730
for this whole movie, right?
- Yeah.

00:03:32.880 --> 00:03:34.980
You know, I've seen Cole multiple times

00:03:34.980 --> 00:03:35.813
throughout the years.

00:03:35.813 --> 00:03:37.800
We met again when he was on "Riverdale"

00:03:37.800 --> 00:03:40.020
and I was on "Supernatural,"
and he kept talking

00:03:40.020 --> 00:03:42.090
about my poodles 'cause
I have these crazy dogs,

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:45.060
and finally I asked you to just shoot,

00:03:45.060 --> 00:03:47.670
and he shot it in my
house with these wigs,

00:03:47.670 --> 00:03:49.770
and it was like you came
up with this narrative,

00:03:49.770 --> 00:03:51.810
like a woman who killed all her husbands,

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.968
and is just collecting dogs
and diamonds, you know?

00:03:54.968 --> 00:03:57.760
And I feel like it was a
precursor to our film, 'cause-

00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.064
- Yeah, I gotta talk to my
therapist about that idea.

00:04:00.064 --> 00:04:00.897
(audience laughing)
- [Kelly] Yeah,

00:04:00.897 --> 00:04:02.040
there's a lot to dive in there.

00:04:02.040 --> 00:04:02.873
- [Kathryn] Yeah.

00:04:02.873 --> 00:04:06.240
- So explain "Lisa Frankenstein"

00:04:06.240 --> 00:04:07.290
to somebody who has never seen it.

00:04:07.290 --> 00:04:08.343
- Oh, did you hear that?

00:04:08.343 --> 00:04:09.360
- He's a fan.

00:04:09.360 --> 00:04:11.970
- Well, how would we explain this movie?

00:04:11.970 --> 00:04:16.230
- I think it's a camp love letter to some

00:04:16.230 --> 00:04:19.170
of that '80s film and television
that we were receiving.

00:04:19.170 --> 00:04:20.220
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:20.220 --> 00:04:21.840
- It deals with grief,

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:24.870
and you get to build your own
boyfriend, which is awesome.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:25.898
I won't say too much.
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:25.898 --> 00:04:26.940
- [Cole] You know, I
can't say too much more.

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:28.125
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:28.125 --> 00:04:28.958
- [Kathryn] He basically got it.

00:04:28.958 --> 00:04:30.450
- Yeah, you build your own boyfriend,

00:04:30.450 --> 00:04:32.280
like Kelly LeBrock in "Weird Science."

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:33.330
- That's right.
- Yeah.

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:34.320
- Yeah, very much like that.

00:04:34.320 --> 00:04:36.060
- That's one of my favorite movies, yeah.

00:04:36.060 --> 00:04:38.040
- It was a really fun,
weird movie to make,

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:41.688
and my costar doesn't speak,
so it was nice for me.

00:04:41.688 --> 00:04:44.160
(audience laughing)

00:04:44.160 --> 00:04:46.320
- It was my favorite
part of our friendship.

00:04:46.320 --> 00:04:48.780
No, that is interesting, you
don't speak in it, right?

00:04:48.780 --> 00:04:49.613
- [Cole] I don't.

00:04:49.613 --> 00:04:52.320
- So that's kind of fun,
like physical like comedy,

00:04:52.320 --> 00:04:53.640
like physical acting, like all that.

00:04:53.640 --> 00:04:55.260
I heard you went to mime school as well.

00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.610
- I worked with a mime.

00:04:56.610 --> 00:04:59.015
- What, did you get out of the box, or?

00:04:59.015 --> 00:05:00.930
(audience laughing)
- Yeah, I'm here.

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:01.763
- [Kelly] You made it.

00:05:01.763 --> 00:05:02.596
- I made it.

00:05:02.596 --> 00:05:05.550
His license plate, he's
an incredible instructor.

00:05:05.550 --> 00:05:07.740
His name's Lorin Salm over in LA.

00:05:07.740 --> 00:05:08.573
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:05:08.573 --> 00:05:09.406
- I knew I was in the right place

00:05:09.406 --> 00:05:12.333
'cause his license plate
just said SPEECHLESS.

00:05:12.333 --> 00:05:13.407
- Oh my God.
(audience laughing)

00:05:13.407 --> 00:05:15.750
- And I was like, "Yeah,
this is probably it."

00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:19.050
But we worked on movement
coaching and all that

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:21.420
for about two to three
months, and then I showed up,

00:05:21.420 --> 00:05:23.670
and I just wanted to help Kathryn out.

00:05:23.670 --> 00:05:25.410
She carries so much of
the weight of the movie,

00:05:25.410 --> 00:05:27.390
that I was like, "I gotta do something.

00:05:27.390 --> 00:05:29.986
I gotta do something if I'm
gonna help her out here."

00:05:29.986 --> 00:05:31.260
- Yeah, yeah, it was weird.

00:05:31.260 --> 00:05:32.289
It's weird to read a script

00:05:32.289 --> 00:05:35.010
and realize that you talk the whole time.

00:05:35.010 --> 00:05:35.843
- Yeah.

00:05:35.843 --> 00:05:37.560
- It's a little daunting, you know?

00:05:37.560 --> 00:05:40.110
But Diablo Cody wrote
the best script ever,

00:05:40.110 --> 00:05:42.975
and Zelda Williams, our
director, she was so,

00:05:42.975 --> 00:05:45.060
it was like the first time
I worked with a director

00:05:45.060 --> 00:05:46.860
where she really had this open dialogue

00:05:46.860 --> 00:05:48.870
and communication to just talk to me

00:05:48.870 --> 00:05:51.900
about everything from the
hair, I really wanted a wig,

00:05:51.900 --> 00:05:54.390
it was a great wig, the
makeup, the wardrobe.

00:05:54.390 --> 00:05:57.120
So it was like I didn't do it alone,

00:05:57.120 --> 00:05:58.890
and I couldn't have done it without Cole.

00:05:58.890 --> 00:06:00.450
Before we filmed, I saw him around,

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:01.710
I'm like, "Are you sure we can do this?"

00:06:01.710 --> 00:06:03.480
And he's like, "We can
do this, I got you."

00:06:03.480 --> 00:06:04.367
And it was really fun.
- Oh, that's cool.

00:06:04.367 --> 00:06:06.090
That's fun to do with friends too.

00:06:06.090 --> 00:06:07.260
- Yeah, it felt like friends.

00:06:07.260 --> 00:06:08.250
It didn't, like it's weird

00:06:08.250 --> 00:06:09.738
that you guys are gonna
watch the movie now,

00:06:09.738 --> 00:06:12.120
'cause it just feels like, I don't know,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:13.350
it's like you do a movie like this,

00:06:13.350 --> 00:06:15.120
and it doesn't feel like
anyone's ever gonna see it.

00:06:15.120 --> 00:06:16.440
You know when you're young and you perform

00:06:16.440 --> 00:06:18.930
for your parents, like after
like with your best friend,

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:20.430
you come up with a routine.
- [Kelly] Totally.

00:06:20.430 --> 00:06:21.352
- [Kathryn] And you do it

00:06:21.352 --> 00:06:22.185
in the living room?
- Yep.

00:06:22.185 --> 00:06:23.281
- I feel like you're all
in my living room now.

00:06:23.281 --> 00:06:24.114
(audience laughing)
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:06:24.114 --> 00:06:25.357
- And gonna watch this movie.
- [Kelly] That was Prince

00:06:25.357 --> 00:06:26.490
"When Doves Cry" for me,

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:28.380
yeah, my dance.
- [Kathryn] Exactly.

00:06:28.380 --> 00:06:29.213
- Yes.

00:06:29.213 --> 00:06:30.720
- And you make your family
watch it, so that's the vibe.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:31.620
- [Kelly] That's awesome.

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:33.810
- Can't say I erupted
in the spontaneous song

00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.550
and dance too often as a child.

00:06:35.550 --> 00:06:37.140
- Gonna be honest with you,
if you catch me in Lowes

00:06:37.140 --> 00:06:39.840
or Target, I'm probably
doing it there too at 41.

00:06:39.840 --> 00:06:40.673
(audience laughing)

00:06:40.673 --> 00:06:42.144
I like to embarrass whoever I'm with,

00:06:42.144 --> 00:06:43.840
just for fun, yeah?
- That's correct,

00:06:43.840 --> 00:06:44.764
yeah, yeah.

00:06:44.764 --> 00:06:45.597
- Yeah.
- I'd get behind that.

00:06:45.597 --> 00:06:47.220
- Just seems like a good time for me.

00:06:47.220 --> 00:06:50.220
Joining us now are the director
and the writer of the film.

00:06:50.220 --> 00:06:52.650
Everybody please welcome Zelda Williams

00:06:52.650 --> 00:06:55.095
and Oscar winning
screenwriter, Diablo Cody.

00:06:55.095 --> 00:07:00.095
(upbeat music)
(audience cheering)

00:07:13.852 --> 00:07:16.440
Oh my God, you were straight up out

00:07:16.440 --> 00:07:18.510
of the coolest '80s movie I've ever seen.

00:07:18.510 --> 00:07:20.790
- It was slightly calculated,
the idea, you know,

00:07:20.790 --> 00:07:21.900
to do the '80s look today,

00:07:21.900 --> 00:07:23.010
but thank you very much, Kelly.

00:07:23.010 --> 00:07:24.148
I'm so excited to meet you.

00:07:24.148 --> 00:07:26.760
- Ditto, I'm such a fan,
y'all are so talented,

00:07:26.760 --> 00:07:28.140
we're very stoked about this movie.

00:07:28.140 --> 00:07:30.158
So where did this movie idea come from?

00:07:30.158 --> 00:07:33.405
- I don't know why, I just
always thought, you know,

00:07:33.405 --> 00:07:35.610
I wanted to write a movie
about a relationship

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:38.067
between a living girl
and a dead dude, and it-

00:07:38.067 --> 00:07:38.900
- [Kelly] Who doesn't?

00:07:38.900 --> 00:07:42.210
- Yeah, I mean, the idea
just kind of knocked around

00:07:42.210 --> 00:07:44.071
in my brain for years, and then COVID hit,

00:07:44.071 --> 00:07:46.170
and I was trapped at
home with three children

00:07:46.170 --> 00:07:47.430
who were suddenly homeschooled,

00:07:47.430 --> 00:07:50.283
which is probably the most
horrifying thing imaginable.

00:07:51.409 --> 00:07:52.350
- It was hard.

00:07:52.350 --> 00:07:53.400
- [Diablo] It was so hard.
- Yeah.

00:07:53.400 --> 00:07:54.930
- So I thought, I have
to escape this at night.

00:07:54.930 --> 00:07:58.230
I'm gonna write this crazy,
freaky, romantic movie.

00:07:58.230 --> 00:07:59.063
- That's nice.

00:07:59.063 --> 00:08:02.400
So you write about
young people like a lot,

00:08:02.400 --> 00:08:04.230
so what were you like as a teen?

00:08:04.230 --> 00:08:06.090
- Not as cool as I thought I was.

00:08:06.090 --> 00:08:07.230
- [Kelly] Okay.
- That's what I'll say.

00:08:07.230 --> 00:08:09.240
- I have not, I didn't think I was cool,

00:08:09.240 --> 00:08:11.190
so I didn't, I was very aware.
- See, I did,

00:08:11.190 --> 00:08:12.060
I was delusional.

00:08:12.060 --> 00:08:12.893
- [Kelly] You did?

00:08:12.893 --> 00:08:13.800
- [Cole] Homeschooled.

00:08:13.800 --> 00:08:14.681
- That's the best.

00:08:14.681 --> 00:08:16.987
What were you like in high school?

00:08:16.987 --> 00:08:19.335
- Not much has changed,
but I was a huge nerd.

00:08:19.335 --> 00:08:20.760
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:08:20.760 --> 00:08:22.132
- I was on the tech committee.

00:08:22.132 --> 00:08:23.340
- [Kelly] Nice, yeah.

00:08:23.340 --> 00:08:24.807
(all laughing)

00:08:24.807 --> 00:08:25.640
That check.
- And I was

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:27.930
in circus club, so-

00:08:27.930 --> 00:08:30.373
- You were a hit, this is amazing.

00:08:30.373 --> 00:08:31.260
(audience laughing)

00:08:31.260 --> 00:08:32.880
Wait, what were you, you loved golf,

00:08:32.880 --> 00:08:34.087
so that obviously kind
of ruled your world?

00:08:34.087 --> 00:08:35.475
- Yeah, I peaked in high school for sure.

00:08:35.475 --> 00:08:36.540
(all laughing)

00:08:36.540 --> 00:08:37.830
It was all downhill from there.

00:08:37.830 --> 00:08:40.740
I loved high school, but I
wasn't there that much, right?

00:08:40.740 --> 00:08:41.573
I wasn't there.

00:08:41.573 --> 00:08:43.200
AcaDeca-
- That's why you loved it.

00:08:43.200 --> 00:08:47.100
- AcaDeca, I ran for class
president, never won.

00:08:47.100 --> 00:08:48.480
I was captain of my golf team,

00:08:48.480 --> 00:08:51.060
which was the best, total
jock, and I was a nerd.

00:08:51.060 --> 00:08:52.500
I was in like the science academy.

00:08:52.500 --> 00:08:53.880
I loved school, yeah.

00:08:53.880 --> 00:08:54.713
- [Kelly] That's awesome.

00:08:54.713 --> 00:08:56.040
- It was good, good time for me.

00:08:56.040 --> 00:08:57.870
- You, homeschooled, weren't you?

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:58.703
- Yeah.

00:08:58.703 --> 00:09:00.422
(all laughing)

00:09:00.422 --> 00:09:02.070
- [Kelly] So you were the
smartest person in your class?

00:09:02.070 --> 00:09:04.530
- Yeah, there was only
one other competition,

00:09:04.530 --> 00:09:06.439
and he wasn't catching up.

00:09:06.439 --> 00:09:08.100
(all laughing)
- He wasn't?

00:09:08.100 --> 00:09:10.380
All right, well, Zelda,
were you a horror fan?

00:09:10.380 --> 00:09:11.213
Have you been into horror?

00:09:11.213 --> 00:09:12.046
- Oh yeah.

00:09:12.046 --> 00:09:14.790
I wasn't allowed to watch
it when I was really young.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:18.030
I was like the kid in my
school where I was allowed

00:09:18.030 --> 00:09:19.440
to see "Shakespeare in Love"

00:09:19.440 --> 00:09:21.900
while everyone else was
watching the horror films.

00:09:21.900 --> 00:09:24.660
But as I got older, I ended
up falling in love with them.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:27.000
I played a monster in
a movie many years ago,

00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:30.465
and that kind of introduced
me to loving all the makeup

00:09:30.465 --> 00:09:33.420
and the crazy transformations.
- The art of it, yeah.

00:09:33.420 --> 00:09:35.358
- The art of it really,
from that point on,

00:09:35.358 --> 00:09:36.810
there was no looking back.

00:09:36.810 --> 00:09:37.643
- Man, I'll tell you what,

00:09:37.643 --> 00:09:39.300
the hair and makeup teams on these movies,

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.980
like they come out and
they transform people,

00:09:40.980 --> 00:09:44.280
it's incredible. the art
department, the sets they create,

00:09:44.280 --> 00:09:45.266
it's an incredible gift.

00:09:45.266 --> 00:09:46.110
- Yeah.

00:09:46.110 --> 00:09:47.400
- This is the only movie I've ever done

00:09:47.400 --> 00:09:50.238
where the male is in the
makeup chair longer than me.

00:09:50.238 --> 00:09:51.990
- That is beautiful.

00:09:51.990 --> 00:09:53.100
- [Kathryn] Yeah, it was nice.

00:09:53.100 --> 00:09:54.390
- And never happens.

00:09:54.390 --> 00:09:55.983
- And he doesn't talk, wow.

00:09:55.983 --> 00:09:56.874
(audience laughs)

00:09:56.874 --> 00:09:59.418
- And he didn't talk, it
was the best date ever.

00:09:59.418 --> 00:10:02.400
Well, I'm gonna ask Kathryn
and Cole, like horror movies,

00:10:02.400 --> 00:10:04.230
