up, were you into those?

00:10:04.230 --> 00:10:05.063
- Oh, huge.

00:10:05.063 --> 00:10:05.896
- [Kelly] Okay.
- Massive.

00:10:05.896 --> 00:10:08.160
- What were like, what's
one of your favorites?

00:10:08.160 --> 00:10:11.640
- My favorite still is John
Carpenter's "The Thing."

00:10:11.640 --> 00:10:13.260
- [Kelly] Oh.
- I mean, to me,

00:10:13.260 --> 00:10:15.480
I fell in love when I was a kid

00:10:15.480 --> 00:10:19.290
with all of the practical
effects and set design,

00:10:19.290 --> 00:10:21.210
and I became a huge monster guy.

00:10:21.210 --> 00:10:22.043
I fell in love

00:10:22.043 --> 00:10:24.172
with all the big "Kaiju"
monster battle movies

00:10:24.172 --> 00:10:25.590
when I was a kid.

00:10:25.590 --> 00:10:28.050
Zelda and I actually share
a lot of the same tastes

00:10:28.050 --> 00:10:30.300
when it comes to monster
movies and stuff like that.

00:10:30.300 --> 00:10:31.800
I'm a big practical effects guy.

00:10:31.800 --> 00:10:34.521
It was one of the reason why,
you know, I read the script,

00:10:34.521 --> 00:10:37.920
and it felt like a
no-brainer for me, truly.

00:10:37.920 --> 00:10:39.076
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- No pun intended.

00:10:39.076 --> 00:10:42.097
- Y'all are-
(all laughing)

00:10:42.097 --> 00:10:43.652
Y'all are probably, very nicely done.

00:10:43.652 --> 00:10:46.140
Y'all are probably too
young, but my, I think

00:10:46.140 --> 00:10:48.011
the scariest thing I saw as a kid was,

00:10:48.011 --> 00:10:51.270
Freddy Krueger was the
scariest thing I ever saw.

00:10:51.270 --> 00:10:53.370
- Freddy Krueger was my guy.

00:10:53.370 --> 00:10:54.840
- Oh my God, we're so different.

00:10:54.840 --> 00:10:55.770
(audience laughing)

00:10:55.770 --> 00:10:57.883
I wouldn't go near a waterbed.

00:10:57.883 --> 00:10:59.222
- [Diablo] Oh, right.

00:10:59.222 --> 00:11:00.360
